<component><section><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.17" extension="2015-08-01"/><code code="29762-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Social history Narrative"/><title>Social History</title><text><list><item>Private pilot who flies a single-engine light aircraft most weekends from a local airfield and hopes to fly longer cross-country trips; holds a third-class FAA medical certificate. Worked as a hospital volunteer before learning to fly and is thinking of returning to pre-medical study [S]</item><item>Works full time in an office on weekdays; lives alone in an apartment; single [S]</item><item>Alcohol: does not drink; no cannabis or other drugs [S]</item><item>Tobacco: never smoked; no vaping; avoids smoky rooms [S]</item><item>Medicines tried: over-the-counter oxymetazoline spray for about two weeks last winter, stopped because the blockage came back worse; a nighttime cold tablet containing diphenhydramine on bad nights, which she did not know is a no-go medicine for pilots [S]</item><item>Supports: her sister and a close friend from the airfield; flying instructors at the airfield. She decides who is told about her health [S]</item></list></text></section></component>

